    {
        "content": "<p><code>3</code> is actually <code>OfNat.ofNat 3</code> (you can see this with <code>set_option pp.explicit true</code>) so the recursor is blocked. <code>dsimp [OfNat.ofNat]</code> is able to make progress.</p>",
        "id": 613637037,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1785415375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's strange that <code>nat_rec</code> don't need it, while recusor does. Any hint why ?</p>",
        "id": 613639436,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1785416132
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>edited : wrong assumption that it was because of irreducible</p>",
        "id": 613643470,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1785417316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For <code>nat_rec</code> it seems to work due to smart unfolding. <code>set_option smartUnfolding false</code> causes it to get stuck on <code>ofNat</code> as well. The primitive recursor goes through a different unfolding path that doesn't use smart unfolding</p>",
        "id": 613644404,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1785417586
    }
]